From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 03:36:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 020/155] [ae-patch] Offer Review after a merge only when it
 was the session's last open pull request

After Merge, a PR card offered "Set this session to review". Review means
the session is done and frees one of Reid's three slots, yet on
2026-09-25 a session that had opened four pull requests showed the offer
after the first merge, while three were still open. The card only asked
the server whether the session was already in review; nothing counted the
session's other pull requests.

The decision now lives in a new file, web/src/lib/aeReviewOffer.ts: after
a merge, take the session's other tracked pull requests (upstream's
per-session list, the one the GitHub panel reads) and read their states
from the same ["ae-pr", repo, number] queries the cards use. Review is
offered only when none is open. While some are open the card says so in a
muted line ("3 more open pull requests in this session.") and offers
nothing; while a state is still unknown it says nothing, so a slow or
failed read never offers review early. The Status submenu still sets
review by hand at any time.

The GitHub panel's cards pass the list they already hold; a card under a
chat message passes the list from the github-info cache when it is there,
and otherwise the hook reads it once, after the merge.

AePrCards.tsx (P12's file) gains the import, the hook call, the muted line,
one condition on the offer and a `tracked` prop; AeInlinePrCards.tsx (also
P12's) passes that prop in one line. No other upstream file is touched.
Suites: aeReviewOffer.test.ts (the pure rule), two cases in
AePrCards.test.tsx (four tracked, first merged: no offer, "3 more"; last
open one merged: offer) and one in AeInlinePrCards.test.tsx.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
